  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "7.0.0\nBreaking:\n- Depends on Microsoft.Data.SqlClient 7. Entra ID (Azure AD) authentication now requires referencing Microsoft.Data.SqlClient.Extensions.Azure in your application.\nNew:\n- net8.0 target (in addition to netstandard2.1).\n- DateOnly/TimeOnly support, including Npgsql 10, which returns DateOnly/TimeOnly for date/time columns.\n- IDataRecord extensions: GetDateOnly, GetTimeOnly, GetTimeSpan, GetDateTimeOffset, GetByteArray, GetEnum.\n- Source generator: DateOnly, TimeOnly, TimeSpan, DateTimeOffset, byte[] and enum properties; error ADONET001 for unsupported property types.\nFixed:\n- Mapping a type with a public property with a non-public setter or getter threw NullReferenceException.\n- Generated mappers cached column ordinals across queries and did not map DBNull to null for nullable reference types.\n- Record constructor mapping conversions, enum conversion, SelectOne key handling, WithParameters with runtime types, chunked GetBytes/GetChars, thread-safety of the query cache.\n- Patched vulnerable transitive dependencies (System.Security.Cryptography.Pkcs, Microsoft.Bcl.Memory).",
